---
// Goal: show an agent builder how an agent calls the ten functions as tools
// through the local MCP server, and how the agent skill helps it pick one.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Code from '../../components/Code.astro';
import { CODE_FUNCTIONS, REPO, MCP } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';

const mcpGuide = `${REPO}/blob/main/libraries/mcp/README.md`;
const mcpSpec = `${REPO}/blob/main/specification/mcp.md`;
const skill = `${REPO}/blob/main/skills/thinkthen/SKILL.md`;
const launch = '{"command": "thinkthen", "args": ["mcp"]}';
const call = `{
  "question": "Does the writer request a refund?",
  "evidence": "Please refund my order."
}`;
---
<Base title="Agents" description="Give an agent the ten ThinkThen functions as tools through the local MCP server, and load the agent skill so it picks the right one.">
  <div class="eyebrow"><a href="/languages/">Languages</a></div>
  <h1>Agents</h1>
  <p class="lede">An agent calls the ten functions as tools. The local MCP server runs them through the same engine and cache as the command line. Use Jev, TypeSafe’s decision model, OpenAI or a local model through the <a href="/models/">backend settings</a>. The agent skill tells the agent which function fits a job.</p>

  <p><strong>Supported versions:</strong> {MCP.versions.runtime}. {MCP.versions.platforms}.</p>

  <h2 id="mcp">The MCP server</h2>
  <p><code>thinkthen mcp</code> serves exactly ten tools over local stdio: {CODE_FUNCTIONS.map((fn, i) => <>{i > 0 && ', '}<a href={`/functions/${fn.name}/`}><code>{fn.name}</code></a></>)}. It starts no shell and no process per call. Each tool returns a typed answer, and a failed call never looks like an answer.</p>
  <p>Install the <a href="/languages/bash/">command</a>, put it on <code>PATH</code>, and set its backend in the environment as you would for the command line. These examples use ThinkThen 0.2 or newer. Check <code>thinkthen mcp --help</code>, then tell your MCP client to launch it:</p>
  <Code code={launch} lang="json" caption="The MCP client's launch entry" label="Copy the launch entry" />
  <p>The server reads the key from the environment, and a tool cannot change the backend or the key. Start options such as <code>--backend</code>, <code>--model</code>, <code>--replay</code> and <code>--no-cache</code> work as they do on the command line. A <code>--replay</code> folder lets an agent's tests run with no key and no network.</p>

  <p><code>tools/list</code> gives compact input guidance for each function. It omits output schemas. Run <code>thinkthen mcp --help</code> for the full argument grammar; the engine checks every call.</p>

  <h2 id="tool-calls">A tool call</h2>
  <p>A <code>decide</code> call takes a question and its evidence:</p>
  <Code code={call} lang="json" caption="The arguments of one decide tool call" label="Copy the decide arguments" />
  <p>A question can also come from a saved <a href="/functions/question-file/">question file</a> through <code>question_file</code>, by name through <code>question_name</code>, or by an <code>@</code> reference through <code>question_reference</code>. A literal question that starts with <code>@</code> stays text and never names a file. The server creates no question files. <code>decide</code>, <code>choose</code> and <code>score</code> also take ordered PNG and JPEG images.</p>
  <p>A tool response carries the complete native call object in <code>structuredContent</code> and the same JSON in a text block. Keep <code>false</code>, <code>null</code> and empty answers as answers. A failed call sets <code>isError</code> and retains its error and any call facts. Incremental failures retain completed records; they do not finish the dataset.</p>
  <p>The <a href={mcpGuide}>MCP guide</a> gives every input and a client with one method for each function. The <a href={mcpSpec}>MCP specification</a> gives the framing and size limits.</p>

  <h2 id="skill">The agent skill</h2>
  <p>The <a href={skill}>ThinkThen skill</a> tells an agent which function fits a job, how to frame evidence, how to read exit codes and not sure, and how to bound requests. Give your agent the skill file <a href={skill}><code>skills/thinkthen/SKILL.md</code></a>.</p>
</Base>
